---
// The Terms of Use and legal disclaimer. A single page that states, in plain language, what the
// publication is, that nothing here is advice, that the data carries no warranty, and that the
// reader's decisions are the reader's own. It reinforces the posture the whole site is built on:
// an impersonal, general-circulation financial publication that informs and never advises. The
// running footer disclaimer on every page is the short form; this is the long form it points to.
//
// Plain register, consistent with /about and the founding letter. Effective date is a fixed
// constant, updated by hand only when the terms themselves change (a legal document's date must
// not move with every deploy).
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { ORG } from "../lib/seo.mjs";

const EFFECTIVE = "July 13, 2026";
const CONTACT = "hello@ownerscorecard.com";
const pageDescription =
  "Terms of Use and disclaimer for Owner Scorecard: an independent financial publication for informational purposes only, not investment advice, with no warranty on the data.";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use, Owner Scorecard"
  description={pageDescription}
  jsonLd={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebPage",
    name: "Owner Scorecard Terms of Use",
    description: pageDescription,
    publisher: ORG,
  }}
>
  <section class="terms">
    <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="eff">Effective {EFFECTIVE}</p>

    <p>
      These terms govern your use of Owner Scorecard (the "Site"), an independent financial
      publication reachable at ownerscorecard.com. By using the Site you agree to these terms. If
      you do not agree, please do not use the Site.
    </p>

    <h2>1. What Owner Scorecard is</h2>
    <p>
      Owner Scorecard is an independent publisher of financial information and research of general
      and regular circulation. It presents the record a company files: roughly a decade of
      revenue, margins, returns on capital, owner earnings, buybacks, share count, and debt, with
      each figure traced to the company's own filings. It is a publication, read the same way by
      everyone, and it is not tailored to any individual's financial situation.
    </p>
    <p>
      Owner Scorecard is not registered as an investment adviser, broker-dealer, or financial
      planner, and it does not act as one. Nothing on the Site creates an advisory, brokerage,
      fiduciary, or other professional or client relationship between you and the publication.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Not investment advice</h2>
    <p>
      Everything on the Site is provided for informational and educational purposes only. Nothing
      on the Site is, or should be taken as, investment, financial, legal, accounting, or tax
      advice, or a recommendation, endorsement, offer, or solicitation to buy, sell, or hold any
      security or to pursue any investment strategy. The Site carries no ratings, price targets,
      or estimates by design, and no figure or page on it is a judgment about what any security is
      worth or whether it should be owned.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Site does not know your circumstances, goals, risk tolerance, or holdings, and nothing
      on it is personalized to you. Any decision you make is your own.
    </p>

    <h2>3. The data, its sources, and its accuracy</h2>
    <p>
      The figures on the Site are drawn from public sources, principally filings made with the
      U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission and the equivalent regulators for the ADR and Japan
      catalogs, together with figures computed from those filings by methods defined on the
      <a href="/concepts">Principles</a> page. These sources are believed to be reliable, but
      their accuracy, completeness, and timeliness are not guaranteed.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Site, and all data, text, and materials on it, are provided "as is" and "as available,"
      without warranty of any kind, whether express or implied, including but not limited to any
      implied warranties of accuracy, completeness, merchantability, fitness for a particular
      purpose, or non-infringement. Filings can contain errors, data can be transcribed or
      computed wrongly, and figures can be out of date. Where an error is found, it is corrected
      in the open and logged in the public <a href="/corrections">corrections record</a>, but no
      promise is made that the Site is free of error. You should verify any figure against the
      company's original filing before relying on it. The primary sources are linked throughout
      the Site for that purpose.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Your decisions are your own</h2>
    <p>
      You are solely responsible for your own investment decisions and their outcomes. Investing
      in securities involves risk, including the possible loss of principal. Past performance is
      not a guarantee or indication of future results. Before making any investment decision you
      should do your own research and consult a qualified professional who can consider your
      individual circumstances. You agree not to treat anything on the Site as a substitute for
      that.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, Owner Scorecard, its founder, and anyone who
      contributes to it will not be liable for any loss or damage of any kind arising out of or in
      connection with your use of, or reliance on, the Site or anything on it. This includes,
      without limitation, any direct, indirect, incidental, consequential, special, punitive, or
      exemplary damages; any trading or investment losses; and any lost profits, lost data, or
      lost opportunities, whether based in contract, tort, negligence, strict liability, or any
      other theory, and whether or not the publication was advised of the possibility of such
      damages. Some jurisdictions do not allow certain of these limitations, and in those places
      the limitations apply to the fullest extent the law allows.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Indemnification</h2>
    <p>
      You agree to indemnify and hold harmless Owner Scorecard and its founder from any claim,
      loss, liability, or expense (including reasonable legal fees) arising out of your use of the
      Site, your breach of these terms, or your violation of any law or the rights of a third
      party.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Positions and disclosure</h2>
    <p>
      The people who write here may own securities discussed on these pages. Positions may change,
      and no position is ever announced, not when it is opened and not when it is closed. Around
      any company the publication writes research on, personal trading stops five days before
      publication and does not resume until ten days after it, and a dated log of every personal
      trade is kept. The reasoning behind these rules is set out in
      <a href="/notes/the-founding-letter">The Founding Letter</a>. Nothing on the Site is written
      to move a price, and the publication earns nothing when you trade.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Use of the Site and its content</h2>
    <p>
      The underlying financial figures come from public filings and are facts, free for anyone to
      use. The Site's own writing, arrangement, computations, and presentation are the property of
      the publication. You are welcome to quote and cite the Site; attribution to Owner Scorecard
      (ownerscorecard.com) is requested but not required, as set out in the
      <a href="/docs/data">data terms</a>. You agree not to use the Site in any way that is
      unlawful, that would disrupt or overburden it, or that would misrepresent it as offering the
      advice it expressly does not offer.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Third-party links</h2>
    <p>
      The Site links to third-party sources, including the SEC's EDGAR system and other filing
      databases. Those sites are not under the publication's control, and the publication is not
      responsible for their content, accuracy, or availability. A link is not an endorsement.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Availability</h2>
    <p>
      The Site is offered free of charge and is provided on an "as available" basis. The
      publication does not guarantee that the Site will be uninterrupted, current, or error-free,
      and it may change, suspend, or discontinue any part of the Site at any time without notice.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      These terms may be updated from time to time. When they change, the effective date above
      will change to say so, and your continued use of the Site after that means you accept the
      updated terms.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of the United States and the state in which the
      publication's founder resides, without regard to conflict-of-laws principles, to the extent
      permitted by applicable law.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>. To
      report a factual error in the data, the <a href="/corrections">corrections record</a>
      describes how errors are handled and fixed.
    </p>

    <p class="fine">
      Owner Scorecard is not registered as an investment adviser or broker-dealer. Nothing here is
      investment advice or a recommendation to buy or sell any security.
    </p>
  </section>

  <style>
    .terms { max-width: 640px; }
    .terms h1 { margin: 0 0 4px; }
    .eff { font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 20px; }
    .terms h2 { margin: 28px 0 10px; font-size: 1.15rem; }
    .terms p { color: var(--ink-soft); }
    .fine { font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 28px; }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
